  "solution": {
    "text": "The given equation can be written as <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mi>y</mi></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mi>y</mi></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> <mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br />Hence, given equation represents two parallel lines"
